                               **VIM**

Text editor:
--> it is a software application used to create, view and modify text files.
eg: VI, VIM, Atom, Nano, Kate

VI??
--> VI stands for Visual Interface

VIM??
--> VIM stands for Vi IMproved
-it is advanced version of VI with more features

**VIM modes:
1. Normal Mode:
--> this is default mode. use 'esc' to switch to normal mode.
--> you can not type or edit text in this mode only we can perform operations here.

2. Insert Mode:
--> this mode is used to type or edit text.
--> use 'i' to enter in insert mode

3. Command Line/ execute Mode:
--> this mode is used to execute commands such as saving,quttting, searching or replacing text.
--> use ':' to type command

4. Visual Mode
--> a mode that provides additional option to select text.
--> use 'v' to enter in visual mode.

**syntax to open file**
vim <file_name>
vim demo.txt

**Saving and quitting**
1. saving a file= :w and press enter
2. exiting vim= :q and press enter
3. saving and quitting= :wq and press enter
4. :set nu = to display line numbers
5. :set nonu = to hide line numbers

**cursor movment shortcuts**
h = move left
j = move down
k = move up
l = move right
   OR
Arrow keys

HW:

gg = move cursor to the begginning of the file
shift +g = move cursor to the last line of the file
shift +h =move cursor to the top of the screen
shift +m = move curesor to the middle of the screen
shift +l =move cursor to the bottom of the screen
<n>gg =move cursor to the nth line
15gg =move cursor to the 15th line of file

**Search and replace**
1. Forward search: (Top to bottom)
syntax: /word
eg: /AWS

press 'n' for the next occurance of the search word

2. Backword search: (bottom to top)
syntax: ?word
eg: ?AWS

Replace:
syntax= :%s/word1/word2/g
--> this command is used to replace word1 with word2 globally.
eg= :%s/AWS/Microsoft Azure/g

hw:
1. current occurance replace
2. replace single occurance defined on number line

**undo and redo**
u = undo last changes
ctrl+r = to redo changes

**Delete, cut, copy and paste**

dd = delete current line
<n>dd = delete n lines from the current line
5dd = delete 5 lines 
dw = delete a word
<n>dw = delete n words

cc = cut the current line
<n>cc = cut n lines
cw = cut the word
<n>cw = cut m words

yy = copy the current line
<n>yy = copy n lines
yw = copy word
<n>yw = copy n words

p = paste cut/copied line
<n>p = paste n times

**Visual Mode**
u = Change the visually selected text to UPPERCASE
shift+u = Change the visually selected text to lowercase
~ = invert the case of visually selected text(lowecase become upeercase and vice versa) 

